 "help": "usage: wgsextract vep download [-h] [--engine {ensembl,vep-rs}] [--species SPECIES]\n                               [--assembly {GRCh37,GRCh38,T2T-CHM13v2.0}]\n                               [--vep-version VEP_VERSION] [--vep-cache VEP_CACHE]\n                               [--mirror {ebi,uk}] [--variations | --no-variations]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --engine {ensembl,vep-rs}\n                        Engine: 'vep-rs' (default; fast Rust VEP, every platform) or 'ensembl'\n                        (Linux, macOS); each has its own cache\n  --species SPECIES     Species name (default: homo_sapiens)\n  --assembly {GRCh37,GRCh38,T2T-CHM13v2.0}\n                        Assembly (default: GRCh38; T2T-CHM13v2.0 with vep-rs)\n  --vep-version VEP_VERSION\n                        Ensembl release version (default: 116)\n  --vep-cache VEP_CACHE\n                        Path to VEP cache directory\n  --mirror {ebi,uk}     Ensembl FTP mirror to use (default: uk)\n  --variations, --no-variations\n                        vep-rs: include known variants (Existing_variation, 1000 Genomes\n                        frequencies, not gnomAD; ~15 GB; default: on)\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract vep download --assembly GRCh38\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  Into the VEP cache directory (vep_cache, or --vep-cache).\n\nneeds:\n  samtools, vep-cache-builder; depending on options and inputs, also: curl,\n  tar; depends on download speed.\n",
